    "Scouting Notes": "One of the most violent swings in baseball. \n It can look pretty unappealing at times, but I actually think it's a better swing than it appears at first glance.\n It sort of reminds me of Mo Vaughn's swing. \n I think by the time he's getting the bat to the hitting zone, a lot of the swing  is right where it should be.\n Shows huge raw power, needs to elevate it a bit more to see the homers\n Pretty decent understanding of the zone and a rare ability to move as well as he does at his size.\n Good athlete who has played some center field, but likely sticks at first base long term.\n Between 2021/2022 he is 37 of 41 on SB attempts, really good baserunner. \n Possible the swing will hamper him as he moves through the system, but I'm not so sure it will. If it does, he could become a non prospect quickly. \n If he can continue to make it work and keep showing his other tools off in game, he can move himself up this list instead.",
